   562	
   563	### 5.3 What dies, stated exactly
   564	
   565	```text
   566	 * NO degree D is emptied, at any range run.  MOH-SHARP-2's D_min >= 105 is neither
   567	   improved nor weakened.
   568	 * NO (B2) or (B3) cell dies.  The filter conditions Moh SKELETONS at a fixed D; a
   569	   campaign cell (N,D) dies only if EVERY skeleton at that D fails for that N, and
   570	   none does.  Case (A) untouched (EMPTY at every N).
   571	 * What dies is the V-assignment (the branch datum).  A surviving skeleton now carries
   572	   not the interval [2,U] for N but an explicit FINITE SET of achievable integers,
   573	   typically of size 1-4.
   574	 * The unconditional kill is nearly as strong as the H2 kill (98.77% vs 98.98% of
   575	   V-assignments at D <= 120): the filter is arithmetic, not window-driven, and does
   576	   NOT depend on the H2 residual.
   577	```
