+# Hostile review: TIME-FUNCTION ENDGAME
+
+**Lane:** `TIME-FUNCTION-ENDGAME`, hostile computational review.  
+**Date:** 2026-09-02.  
+**Scope:** the nine charged items, the selected `D = 105` arithmetic candidate,
+the 15-row star-existence computation plus two extensions, three control suites,
+and the DELTA-DENOM measurement. No ledger was edited and `jc2-lean` was not used.
+
+For compact citations below, `TF` means the frozen
+`time-function-endgame-opus5-20260902.md`, `I17` the frozen integration report,
+and `D1` the frozen `d1-subtree-opus5-20260902.md`. Driver citations name the
+file in `box/tfe-drivers-20260902/`; the frozen `d1floor.py` is cited explicitly.
+
+## 0. Executive verdict
+
+The leading bottom-disc Wronskian is real and useful. BOTTOM-ODE,
+STAR-SIMPLE, STAR-SUM, and STAR-ABC survive hostile reproof. The flagship as a
+whole does not: its local formal equation is not equivalent to the global
+Lagrange/polynomiality problem; one displayed STAR-RESIDUE normalization is
+wrong; STAR-EIGEN has a concrete `A = 1` counterexample; and the advertised
+resonant order-two calculation feeds a quadratic source to the wrong exponent.
+The exact restricted linear map has only three positive resonances, not all of
+`mu Z_{>0}`. Outer-root factors also violate the degree caps used to call that
+map the full coefficient problem.
+
+The existence computation does certify 15/15 proper augmented ideals, and two
+more cases with `b_1` equal to 8 and 7 are likewise realisable. It does not
+provide explicit coordinate witnesses for all 15. The `D = 105` counts are
+consistent after separating lower-`V` assignments from Moh groups and after
+separating `[4,16]` from `[6,16]`. The selected row *admits* `k = 20`, `N = 6`
+arithmetically; neither the picker nor D1-PIN proves attainment of 20 actual
+bottom discs.
+
+| item | hostile verdict | promotion |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1. LOCAL-KELLER / interpolation | **GAP** | **CAN** promote the exact necessary disc identity; **CANNOT** promote equivalence to global interpolation and `C[x]` polynomiality |
+| 2. BOTTOM-ODE and `kappa` | **CONFIRMED** | **CAN** |
+| 3. STAR-SIMPLE / RESIDUE / SUM | **GAP as bundled** | SIMPLE and SUM **CAN**; RESIDUE **CAN after one formula correction** |
+| 4. STAR-ABC / dessin | **CONFIRMED** | **CAN**, with the converse degree step made explicit |
+| 5. STAR-EIGEN | **REFUTED as displayed** | **CANNOT** as written; repaired `A > 1` dichotomy and all-`A` divisibility **CAN** |
+| 6. `D = 105` resonance endgame | **REFUTED as charged** | restricted matrix/rank facts **CAN**; claimed recurrence, full dimension, and no-kill conclusion **CANNOT** |
+| 7. Nullstellensatz table | **GAP as bundled** | 15/15 existence decisions **CAN**; “explicit witnesses for all 15” **CANNOT** |
+| 8. controls 78/0 | **GAP in one printed table** | controls 1 and 3 **CAN**; two-tower qualitative failure **CAN after correcting `lambda_g`** |
+| 9. DELTA-DENOM measurement | **CONFIRMED as measurement** | **CAN** as a measurement only; no filter adjudicated here |
+| `D = 105` selection/counts | **GAP if read as attainment** | census arithmetic **CAN**; “there are 20 discs, hence `N=6`” **CANNOT** |
+
+## 1. Custody and reproduction
+
+The mandatory hash gate was run before opening the inputs. All five hashes
+matched exactly:
+
+```text
+9f47a25fb7ceb0174add0f0c245d1e9bca914cadb108053bb02abf714bf685c1  time-function-endgame-opus5-20260902.md
+126d9c84b7ee373891e4e40f8a60b25495a4e0ed89da9c6febe5224a461686f5  integration17-coordinator-fable51-20260902.md
+26479b06b0f1ef526fe37bd34bccb61f50f207a509fcb0b0c1ae6fc5751858c0  d1-subtree-opus5-20260902.md
+69ff5bdea265adc37c9518f381eccfe6a6162c430a51075b6c2069f709894473  bottomode.py
+cf0780cc0b3ef0f2de630e6901f836596c1dd58e3ff1dc0917e9c8d363baebe6  d1floor.py
+```
+
+The full SHA-256 values of the live drivers begin with exactly the abbreviations
+declared at `TF:39-42`; in particular `orders.py = 43904846...`, `order2.py =
+42f125a6...`, `starexist.py = 39e742b3...`, and controls 1--4 are
+`c698da00...`, `71219169...`, `5c04bec2...`, `f2ea1b3d...`. The live
+`bottomode.py` and the frozen copy are identical, as are the live and frozen
+`d1floor.py`.
+
+All exact CAS runs used Python/SymPy over `QQ` with
+`OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=OMP_NUM_THREADS=MKL_NUM_THREADS=1`. The delivered
+`orders.py` and `order2.py` outputs reproduced their checked-in logs byte for
+byte. I separately constructed the order-one matrix and order-two source in a
+fresh SymPy snippet rather than importing either result. Controls 1, 3, and 4
+were rerun (57 checks). The star ideals were rerun in one-core mode, with an
+explicit ring/generator audit and positive and negative saturation controls.
+
+## 2. From JAC-FIBRE to the exact local identity
+
+### 2.1 What JAC-FIBRE really gives
+
+Let `g(x,tau_i(x)) = c_2` on a simple branch of a generic fibre. Then
+
+```text
+g_x + g_y tau_i' = 0,
+d/dx f(x,tau_i) = f_x + f_y tau_i' = (f_x g_y - f_y g_x)/g_y = c/g_y.
+```
+
+Thus, for a pre-existing Keller pair,
+
+```text
+f(x,tau_i(x)) = c integral dx/g_y(x,tau_i(x)) + a_i.
+```
+
+This is the exact series identity behind the promoted valuation statement
+`I17:14-17` and `D1:203-214`. Since `g-c_2` is monic with `n` distinct generic
+roots and `deg_y f=m<n`, `f` is indeed the unique degree-`<n` Lagrange
+interpolant through these `n` values. That global programme is stated at
+`I17:94-100`.
+
+Now put
+
+```text
+x=t^(-1),                 y=w(t)+pi t^delta,
+F(t,pi)=f(x,y),           G(t,pi)=g(x,y).
+```
+
+The change-of-variables determinant is
+
+```text
+det d(x,y)/d(t,pi) = -t^(delta-2),
+```
+
+so the full polynomial Jacobian, not merely its valuation, gives
+
+```text
+F_t G_pi - F_pi G_t = -c t^(delta-2).                         (2.1)
+```
+
+Write `F=t^lambda_f Phi`, `G=t^lambda_g Gamma`. Without assuming order
+matching, the exact normalized equation is
+
+```text
+(lambda_f Phi+t Phi_t) Gamma_pi
+ -(lambda_g Gamma+t Gamma_t) Phi_pi
+ = -c t^[delta-1-(lambda_f+lambda_g)].                        (2.2)
+```
+
+At a bottom disc, D1-PIN supplies
+`lambda_f+lambda_g=delta_1-1`; see `D1:328-350` and the independent radius
+formulas at `D1:143-158`. Therefore the exponent on the right of (2.2) is zero,
+and `TF:202-213` is exact coefficient by coefficient:
+
+```text
+(lambda_f Phi+t Phi_t) Gamma_pi
+ -(lambda_g Gamma+t Gamma_t) Phi_pi = -c.                     (LOCAL-KELLER)
+```
+
+This answers one mandatory question narrowly and positively: the
+one-variable Keller equation is the leading-order bracket in the disc
+coordinate `pi`, and the untruncated bracket identity is exact for an actual
+Keller pair.
+
+### 2.2 Why item 1 is still a GAP
+
+`TF:234-238` says that coefficients polynomial in `x` are the same as
+`Phi,Gamma in C[[t^eta]][pi]`, and concludes that all coefficient equations are
+the conjunction of interpolation conditions (i)--(ii). That identification is
+false. The completed Puiseux ring permits arbitrary infinite fractional-power
+tails. It does not say that the Lagrange coefficients lie in `C[x]`; it does not
+glue constants `a_i` under monodromy; and it does not enforce compatibility
+among all `n=105` branches or among the candidate bottom discs. The report's
+own `TF:715-718` correctly concedes that a local solution is not attainment of
+a Keller pair.
+
+There is a second overstatement at `TF:215-218`: bare order mismatch need not
+make (2.1) unsatisfiable. If the nominal leading bracket is earlier than the
+Jacobian order, its leading coefficient can vanish and the constant Jacobian
+can occur later. `TF:220-222` invokes exactly that sub-leading behaviour at
+higher discs. At `D_1` there is no damage because D1-PIN independently proves
+the equality; it should not be re-derived from an order comparison that has
+not excluded cancellation.
+
+**Line repair for `TF:234-238`:**
+
+> For a pre-existing Keller polynomial pair, LOCAL-KELLER is an exact necessary
+> identity in the completed bottom-disc ring and gives a coefficient equation
+> at every exponent. Membership in that completed ring is only local formal
+> regularity/no-log. Polynomiality of the global Lagrange interpolant in `x`,
+> compatibility of the `n` branch constants, and inter-disc gluing remain
+> separate conditions.
+
+Verdict: **GAP** for the charged equivalence; **CONFIRMED/CAN** for the exact
+necessary coordinate identity.
+
+## 3. BOTTOM-ODE and the normalization of `kappa`
+
+At order zero put `Phi_0=p_f`, `Gamma_0=p_g`. LOCAL-KELLER gives
+
+```text
+lambda_f p_f p_g' - lambda_g p_g p_f' = -c.                  (3.1)
+```
+
+Moh's level-one proportionality is
+`lambda_f/lambda_g=m/n=d/e`, while Def. 5.1(1) gives
+
+```text
+deg p_g = a_1=e V_2,        deg p_f=b_1=d V_2;
+```
+
+see `D1:136-155`. Multiplying (3.1) by `e/lambda_g` yields
+
+```text
+d p_f p_g' - e p_g p_f' = kappa,      kappa=-e c/lambda_g.  (3.2)
+```
+
+Since
+
+```text
+lambda_g(delta_1) = -e(1-delta_1)/(d+e),
+q = (1-delta_1)de/(d+e),
+```
+
+one obtains exactly
+
+```text
+kappa = c(d+e)/(1-delta_1) = c d e/q != 0.                  (3.3)
+```
+
+This confirms the sign, degrees, and all three correct expressions in
+`TF:242-253`.
+
+For the mandatory control `(f,g)=(y,x+y^k)`, with the convention
+`[f,g]=f_xg_y-f_yg_x`,
+
+```text
+c=-1, delta_1=-1/k, (d,e,V_2)=(1,k,1), q=1,
+p_f=pi, p_g=1+pi^k,
+p_f p_g' - k p_g p_f' = -k = cde/q.
+```
+
+This independently confirms `TF:259-262`; controls `k=2,...,7` reproduce it.
+
+The delivered `bottomode.py` also reproduces the selected `(2,3,1)` coefficient
+system. On its nondegenerate component,
+
+```text
+p_g=pi^3+p_1 pi,
+p_f=q_2(pi^2+(2/3)p_1),
+kappa=(4/3)p_1^2 q_2,       p_1 q_2 != 0.
+```
+
+SymPy also prints a component with `q_2=0`; it violates `deg p_f=2` and has
+`kappa=0`, so it is correctly discarded. One driver-description caveat:
+`bottomode.py:63-78` contains only `pass` where a dimension computation is
+described. The one-orbit conclusion follows from the displayed exact normal
+form, not from that function.
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED — CAN promote.**
