+## 9. Nullstellensatz existence table
+
+The construction in `star.py:38-47` uses a monic, translation-normalized
+`Q=p_f` of degree `b=dV`, expands `Q^(e/d)` at infinity, kills coefficients
+`pi^-1,...,pi^[-(b-2)]`, and takes its polynomial part as `P=p_g`. If the
+remainder begins at `pi^[-(b-1)]`, differentiating shows
+`dQP'-ePQ'` is a polynomial of degree at most zero. Thus it is legitimate to
+use its constant coefficient `kappa` in the Rabinowitsch equation.
