+# Hostile review: TIME-FUNCTION ENDGAME
+
+**Lane:** `TIME-FUNCTION-ENDGAME`, hostile computational review.  
+**Date:** 2026-09-02.  
+**Scope:** the nine charged items, the selected `D = 105` arithmetic candidate,
+the 15-row star-existence computation plus two extensions, three control suites,
+and the DELTA-DENOM measurement. No ledger was edited and `jc2-lean` was not used.
+
+For compact citations below, `TF` means the frozen
+`time-function-endgame-opus5-20260902.md`, `I17` the frozen integration report,
+and `D1` the frozen `d1-subtree-opus5-20260902.md`. Driver citations name the
+file in `box/tfe-drivers-20260902/`; the frozen `d1floor.py` is cited explicitly.
+
+## 0. Executive verdict
+
+The leading bottom-disc Wronskian is real and useful. BOTTOM-ODE,
+STAR-SIMPLE, STAR-SUM, and STAR-ABC survive hostile reproof. The flagship as a
+whole does not: its local formal equation is not equivalent to the global
+Lagrange/polynomiality problem; one displayed STAR-RESIDUE normalization is
+wrong; STAR-EIGEN has a concrete `A = 1` counterexample; and the advertised
+resonant order-two calculation feeds a quadratic source to the wrong exponent.
+The exact restricted linear map has only three positive resonances, not all of
+`mu Z_{>0}`. Outer-root factors also violate the degree caps used to call that
+map the full coefficient problem.
+
+The existence computation does certify 15/15 proper augmented ideals, and two
+more cases with `b_1` equal to 8 and 7 are likewise realisable. It does not
+provide explicit coordinate witnesses for all 15. The `D = 105` counts are
+consistent after separating lower-`V` assignments from Moh groups and after
+separating `[4,16]` from `[6,16]`. The selected row *admits* `k = 20`, `N = 6`
+arithmetically; neither the picker nor D1-PIN proves attainment of 20 actual
+bottom discs.
+
+| item | hostile verdict | promotion |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1. LOCAL-KELLER / interpolation | **GAP** | **CAN** promote the exact necessary disc identity; **CANNOT** promote equivalence to global interpolation and `C[x]` polynomiality |
+| 2. BOTTOM-ODE and `kappa` | **CONFIRMED** | **CAN** |
+| 3. STAR-SIMPLE / RESIDUE / SUM | **GAP as bundled** | SIMPLE and SUM **CAN**; RESIDUE **CAN after one formula correction** |
+| 4. STAR-ABC / dessin | **CONFIRMED** | **CAN**, with the converse degree step made explicit |
