+The leading bottom-disc Wronskian is real and useful. BOTTOM-ODE,
+STAR-SIMPLE, STAR-SUM, and STAR-ABC survive hostile reproof. The flagship as a
+whole does not: its local formal equation is not equivalent to the global
+Lagrange/polynomiality problem; one displayed STAR-RESIDUE normalization is
+wrong; STAR-EIGEN has a concrete `A = 1` counterexample; and the advertised
+resonant order-two calculation feeds a quadratic source to the wrong exponent.
+The exact restricted linear map has only three positive resonances, not all of
+`mu Z_{>0}`. Outer-root factors also violate the degree caps used to call that
