+# Hostile review: TIME-FUNCTION ENDGAME
+
+**Lane:** `TIME-FUNCTION-ENDGAME`, hostile computational review.  
+**Date:** 2026-09-02.  
+**Scope:** the nine charged items, the selected `D = 105` arithmetic candidate,
+the 15-row star-existence computation plus two extensions, three control suites,
+and the DELTA-DENOM measurement. No ledger was edited and `jc2-lean` was not used.
+
+For compact citations below, `TF` means the frozen
+`time-function-endgame-opus5-20260902.md`, `I17` the frozen integration report,
+and `D1` the frozen `d1-subtree-opus5-20260902.md`. Driver citations name the
+file in `box/tfe-drivers-20260902/`; the frozen `d1floor.py` is cited explicitly.
+
+## 0. Executive verdict
+
+BOTTOM-ODE, STAR-SIMPLE, STAR-SUM, and STAR-ABC survive reproof. The full
+flagship does not: local completion is not global polynomial interpolation;
+STAR-RESIDUE has one bad normalization; STAR-EIGEN fails at `A=1`; and the
+order-two driver sends its source to the wrong exponents. The restricted map
+has three positive resonances, not `mu Z_{>0}`, and omits visible outer-root
+degrees. The 15 existence decisions and two extensions pass, but explicit
+points for all 15 were not delivered. The `D=105` counts reconcile by type and
+threshold; `k=20,N=6` is arithmetically permitted, not attained.
+
+The full typed verdict is in section 13.
+
+## 1. Custody and reproduction
+
+The mandatory hash gate was run before opening the inputs. All five hashes
+matched exactly:
+
+```text
+9f47a25fb7ceb0174add0f0c245d1e9bca914cadb108053bb02abf714bf685c1  time-function-endgame-opus5-20260902.md
