+```
+
+so neither claimed root alternative holds; its Wronskian is nevertheless the
+nonzero constant `35/27`. `starcheck.py:89-94` checks only congruences modulo
+`A`; modulo 1 both alternatives are vacuous, so its “case 1” label does not
+test the bracketed root claim.
